From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 22:03:28 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Assert on the IEJoin predicate without an assert-only binding

IEJoinLocalSourceState::ApplyArbitraryPredicate() binds the operator
to a name that only D_ASSERT() reads, so in a release build, where
D_ASSERT() expands to nothing, the binding is unused and
-Wunused-variable says so. The assertion reads the operator through
the source state and the binding goes, which is the shape upstream
gives the function later.

Carried here until the engine brings the same change.

---
 src/duckdb/src/execution/operator/join/physical_iejoin.cpp | 3 +--
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/duckdb/src/execution/operator/join/physical_iejoin.cpp b/src/duckdb/src/execution/operator/join/physical_iejoin.cpp
index 424052e880..e6be544b1a 100644
--- a/src/duckdb/src/execution/operator/join/physical_iejoin.cpp
+++ b/src/duckdb/src/execution/operator/join/physical_iejoin.cpp
@@ -1385,8 +1385,7 @@ void IEJoinLocalSourceState::SplitPayloads(DataChunk &chunk) {
 
 const SelectionVector *IEJoinLocalSourceState::ApplyArbitraryPredicate(DataChunk &chunk) {
 	//	Apply any arbitrary predicate
-	auto &op = gsource.op;
-	D_ASSERT(op.predicate);
+	D_ASSERT(gsource.op.predicate);
 
 	const auto result_count = pred_executor.SelectExpression(chunk, pred_matches);
 	chunk.Slice(pred_matches, result_count);
